---
import runtime from '../runtime.json';
import '../styles/site.css';
---
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>isotrail</title>
<script is:inline type="module" src={`${runtime.path}isotrail-embed.js`}></script>
</head>
<body data-runtime={runtime.path}>
<main>
<h1>isotrail</h1>
<p>Turn a GPX file into a pixel-art 3D diorama, in your browser. The file never leaves it.</p>
<p>Choose a GPX file. The scene is built on this page. Only the elevation, map and weather services are asked for data. Their answers are kept in the browser, so a second build downloads nothing.</p>
<label>Options, as <code>isotrail render</code> flag names
  <textarea id="options" rows="3" spellcheck="false">{'{}'}</textarea>
</label>
<label>GPX file <input type="file" id="file" accept=".gpx"></label>
<p><button id="cancel" type="button" disabled>Cancel</button></p>
<p id="status" role="status">No file yet.</p>
<p><a id="download" hidden>Download the scene file</a></p>
<p><span id="cache">Cache: counting…</span> <button id="clear" type="button">Clear the cache</button></p>
<isotrail-hike id="hike" aspect="wide"></isotrail-hike>
</main>
<script>
  import '../scripts/scene.js';
</script>
</body>
</html>
